      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Todd is offering a beautiful five-bedroom detached property with a conseratory and blocked garage set on a generous 0.75 acre site in Ardskea Beg, Ballyglunin, Co. Galway.\n\nAs you enter through the front door, you'll be greeted by a hallway adorned with cream porcelain tiled floor, exuding elegance and sophistication. The hallway is illuminated with lighting, creating a warm and inviting ambiance.\n\nTo the left of the hallway, you'll find a spacious living room boasting a bay window, solid oak floors and a marble fireplace. This generous area is perfect for relaxing, entertaining guests, or enjoying family time. The bay window allows natural light to flood the room, creating a bright and welcoming atmosphere. Glass double doors enter out into the large kitchen dining area. The stunning kitchen dining area is a true delight, featuring handcrafted oak units and exquisite worktop with stand alone island. The combination of these high-quality materials adds a touch of luxury to the heart of the home. It's the perfect setting for preparing meals, enjoying family dinners, and entertaining guests. Just off the dining area is south west facing conservatory where one can enjoy on a sunny day. Adjacent to the kitchen, you'll find a utility room equipped with a sink, washing machine, and dryer. This area is designed to provide convenience and functionality, making household chores a breeze. Additionally, the ground floor offers a well-placed downstairs toilet and cloakroom, ensuring convenience for both residents and visitors. To the right of the hallway, you'll discover a generously sized sitting room / downstairs bedroom. This additional space provides versatility and can be used as a cosy retreat for reading, as a play area, bedroom or even as a home office. Moving upstairs, a carpeted staircase with solid oak banisters leads you to four large double bedrooms. Two of these bedrooms features an ensuite and one with walk in wardrobe, providing privacy and comfort. The main bathroom, equipped with high-quality fixtures and fittings, is tastefully designed with tiled flooring that extends from the floor to the ceiling, creating a sleek and modern look. Upstairs has holocore flooring installed and there are heating controls installed thoughout the house. Furthermore, the attic of this property has been floored offering additional storage space. A spacious garage with a roller door is included, offering ample storage space for vehicle, tools, and other belongings. Outside, the property boasts neatly laid lawns and mature laurel hedging for privacy, enhancing the aesthetic appeal of the surroundings. Kerbing adds a finishing touch to the exterior, creating a well-maintained and visually appealing property. There are two solar panels fitted that heat the water. In conclusion, this five-bedroom detached property offers a harmonious blend of style, functionality, and luxury. It provides a warm and inviting atmosphere, along with ample living space and a range of attractive features. As future homeowners, it's important to consider the layout, design, and practicality of a property, and this one appears to tick all the right boxes.\nExcellent locatation only 1min drive from Corrofin village, 10min to Tuam and 20mins to Galway City. The M17 motorway access is only 5mins away via the Roscommon exit. Viewing is highly recommended. Please contact Sherry FitzGerald today on 09326622 to arrange a viewing appointment."
      },
